   "start": 1924,
   "end": 1951,
   "text": "# Damiao Motors and CAN Bus",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 1,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 1953,
   "end": 2043,
   "text": "This guide covers setup and usage of Damiao motors with LeRobot via CAN bus communication.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2045,
   "end": 2136,
   "text": "Currently, only Linux is supported, as the OpenArms CAN adapter only has drivers for Linux.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2138,
   "end": 2156,
   "text": "## Linux CAN Setup",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2158,
   "end": 2244,
   "text": "Before using Damiao motors, you need to set up the CAN interface on your Linux system.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2246,
   "end": 2271,
   "text": "### Install CAN Utilities",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2317,
   "end": 2353,
   "text": "### Configure CAN Interface (Manual)",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2355,
   "end": 2402,
   "text": "For standard CAN FD (recommended for OpenArms):",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2539,
   "end": 2569,
   "text": "For standard CAN (without FD):",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2683,
   "end": 2726,
   "text": "### Configure CAN Interface (Using LeRobot)",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2728,
   "end": 2795,
   "text": "LeRobot provides a utility script to setup and test CAN interfaces:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2936,
   "end": 2966,
   "text": "## Debugging CAN Communication",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2968,
   "end": 3025,
   "text": "Use the built-in debug tools to test motor communication:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3200,
   "end": 3297,
   "text": "The test mode will scan for motors (IDs 0x01-0x08) and report which ones respond. Example output:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 3500,
   "end": 3508,
   "text": "## Usage",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 3510,
   "end": 3525,
   "text": "### Basic Setup",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 4029,
   "end": 4053,
   "text": "### Reading Motor States",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 17,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 4491,
   "end": 4517,
   "text": "### Writing Motor Commands",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 4822,
   "end": 4846,
   "text": "## Configuration Options",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 19,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 4848,
   "end": 4940,
   "text": "| Parameter      | Default   | Description                                                 |",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 5034,
   "end": 5126,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧         | -         | CAN interface (⟦1⟧) or serial port (⟦2⟧) |",
   "tokens": [
    "`port`",
    "`can0`",
    "`/dev/cu.usbmodem*`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 5127,
   "end": 5219,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧   | ⟦1⟧    | Enable CAN FD for higher data rates                         |",
   "tokens": [
    "`use_can_fd`",
    "`True`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 22,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 5220,
   "end": 5312,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧      | ⟦1⟧ | Nominal bitrate (1 Mbps)                                    |",
   "tokens": [
    "`bitrate`",
    "`1000000`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 23,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 5313,
   "end": 5405,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧ | ⟦1⟧ | CAN FD data bitrate (5 Mbps)                                |",
   "tokens": [
    "`data_bitrate`",
    "`5000000`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 5407,
   "end": 5429,
   "text": "## Motor Configuration",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 5431,
   "end": 5451,
   "text": "Each motor requires:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 5453,
   "end": 5488,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧: CAN ID for sending commands",
   "tokens": [
    "`id`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 27,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 5489,
   "end": 5568,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧: One of the supported motor types (e.g., ⟦1⟧, ⟦2⟧)",
   "tokens": [
    "`motor_type`",
    "`\"dm8009\"`",
    "`\"dm4340\"`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 28,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 5569,
   "end": 5612,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧: CAN ID for receiving responses",
   "tokens": [
    "`recv_id`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 29,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 5614,
   "end": 5717,
   "text": "OpenArms default IDs follow the pattern: send ID ⟦0⟧, receive ID ⟦1⟧ where N is the joint number.",
   "tokens": [
    "`0x0N`",
    "`0x1N`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 30,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 5719,
   "end": 5737,
   "text": "## Troubleshooting",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 31,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 5739,
   "end": 5766,
   "text": "### No Response from Motors",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 32,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 5768,
   "end": 5786,
   "text": "1. **Check power**",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 33,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 5787,
   "end": 5852,
   "text": "2. **Verify CAN wiring**: Check CAN-H, CAN-L, and GND connections",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 34,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 5853,
   "end": 5927,
   "text": "3. **Check motor IDs**: Use Damiao Debugging Tools to verify/configure IDs",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 35,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 5928,
   "end": 6011,
   "text": "4. **Test CAN interface**: Run ⟦0⟧ to see if messages are being received",
   "tokens": [
    "`candump can0`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 36,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 6012,
   "end": 6085,
   "text": "5. **Run diagnostics**: ⟦0⟧",
   "tokens": [
    "`lerobot-setup-can --mode=test --interfaces=can0`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 37,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 6087,
   "end": 6114,
   "text": "### Motor Timeout Parameter",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 38,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 6116,
   "end": 6249,
   "text": "If motors were configured with timeout=0, they won't respond to commands. Use Damiao Debugging Tools to set a non-zero timeout value.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 39,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 6251,
   "end": 6275,
   "text": "### Verify CAN FD Status",
   "tokens": []
  }
 ]
}